    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41136" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕnūtus</span></b> ,
		ūs, m.
		renuo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a denying</i>, <i>refusal;</i> a word formed by
			Pliny the Younger, for the Homeric <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνένευσεν</span> (Il. 16, 250): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ego quoque simili nutu ac renutu respondere
					voto tuo possum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 1, 7, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
